 "style": {
  "name": "Taiga Service Corridor",
  "rationale": "Second pass: the heavy grey roof slab that dominated the render is now a timber ceiling section of dark-oak beams over coffers recessed 1 block, with stripped-spruce ribs and a log band on the cut face. Each post now carries a knee brace and two side brackets. The far wall's relief is layered: a deepslate stair plinth, panels set flush, polished niches recessed with tile lintels, and an overhanging spruce-stair cornice over a two-course stripped-spruce frieze. The floor is now patterned, with polished-deepslate bands under each post, a tile field and a polished edge at the section. The redstone channel is cut 1 block down, lined with smooth stone, and has a repeater at every post. Lanterns hang on 2 chain links over the channel. Barrels, chests and potted plants alternate in the niches. The 3-wide walk is kept clear."
 },
